WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.020
There are so many new beauty products

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.440
being released all the time,

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.131
so we gathered some of the most hyped

00:00:11.131 --> 00:00:12.497
to test for ourselves.

00:00:12.497 --> 00:00:14.633
First up, we have the L'Oréal Fresh Wear

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:16.210
Foundation in a Powder.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.170
I have zero experience
with powder foundations,

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.930
so this one made me nervous.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.637
This stuff is full coverage.

00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:27.020
Like, covered all of my dark
spots and acne, no problem.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.130
The application was surprisingly smooth

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.050
and I didn't notice any dry patches,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.103
and all of my other products
layered so well over it.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.910
Here's what it looked
like eight hours later.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:38.950
I did get oily,

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:42.248
but I still feel like the
foundation looks beautiful.

00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:44.524
The EcoTools BioBlender Makeup Sponge

00:00:44.524 --> 00:00:47.310
is a 100% biodegradable makeup sponge,

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.050
which is so exciting!

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.990
This sponge blends really, really well.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.820
It's a bit firmer in
texture, but I didn't mind.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.120
And the shape lets you get into

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.753
those hard-to-blend areas.

00:00:56.753 --> 00:00:59.360
It's recommended that you
compost it after 30 days,

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.040
which at 5 bucks a sponge isn't terrible.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.790
It also comes in 100% plantable packaging,

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.580
which is such a cool touch.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.505
The Sally Hansen Hydrate Peel-Off

00:01:08.505 --> 00:01:10.421
Nail Mask Treatment is like a little tiny

00:01:10.421 --> 00:01:12.410
peel-off mask for each of your nails.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.880
It's meant to relieve
dry nails and cuticles.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.510
You just apply a layer to each nail

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:18.590
and peel off after 15 minutes.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.440
I definitely did too thick
of a layer on my nails,

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.000
so it didn't peel perfectly,

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.420
but my nails and cuticles
felt nice afterwards.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.200
It does feel like a
gimmicky sort of product,

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.491
but still fun to use.

00:01:30.491 --> 00:01:33.872
I finally got my hands
on the ABH Brow Freeze,

00:01:33.872 --> 00:01:35.197
and there is a reason why

00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:36.860
this stuff is sold out everywhere.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.070
This stuff is amazing.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.361
It definitely gives your brows

00:01:39.361 --> 00:01:41.136
that laminated, fluffy look

00:01:41.136 --> 00:01:43.220
with little to no effort.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.540
This is what it looks like
on my brows with no makeup,

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.170
I just wanted to see how it made them look

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.410
without filling them in,
and they look so full.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.320
It also has serious staying power.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.900
Here's what my brows looked
like at the end of the day,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.023
and there's not a hair out of place.

00:01:57.023 --> 00:02:00.240
The Ordinary Concealer
claims to be full coverage,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.040
but I feel like it's more medium.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.530
You could probably build
this up if you wanted to.

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.370
I definitely got the wrong shade

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.890
because my skin hasn't
seen the sun in ages,

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:10.950
but I'm not super in love with this.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.575
I feel like my dark under eyes

00:02:12.575 --> 00:02:13.808
weren't super covered,

00:02:13.808 --> 00:02:16.740
and I hate this sort of
packaging for concealers.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.735
I just feel like I've
tried better concealers

00:02:18.735 --> 00:02:20.580
at this $5 price point.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.402
But one great thing is that it does have

00:02:22.402 --> 00:02:25.680
a diverse range of shades and undertones.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.521
I was so excited to try out

00:02:27.521 --> 00:02:28.871
the Milk Makeup Color Chalk

00:02:28.871 --> 00:02:31.255
because Milk is one of my favorite brands,

00:02:31.255 --> 00:02:33.410
but I think this one is a miss.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.235
It's definitely...a chalk.

00:02:36.235 --> 00:02:37.278
It's pretty dry,

00:02:37.278 --> 00:02:39.150
and it needs some
moisture to spread easier,

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.160
so I used my setting spray to help.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.026
I feel like I had to apply a lot

00:02:43.026 --> 00:02:44.650
to get the payoff that I wanted,

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.500
which normally wouldn't bother me,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.534
but this thing is so
tiny it's unbelievable.

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:52.503
Like, this tiny thing costs $18.

00:02:52.503 --> 00:02:54.130
The packaging is also kind of messy,

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.350
but it is refillable, which I like.

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:57.691
And I actually ended up loving

00:02:57.691 --> 00:02:59.782
this coppery orange color.

